 "capsule": "The 8 March 1963 coup brought the Arab Socialist Ba'ath Party to power in Syria, installing a National Council of the Revolutionary Command, with Amin al-Hafiz emerging as head of state by July 1963 while the military committee of Muhammad Umran, Salah Jadid, and Hafez al-Assad purged rival officers and replaced most of the officer corps with Ba'athist loyalists. This new one-party state pursued Arab-nationalist and socialist land and industry nationalizations until Syria's defeat in the June 1967 Six-Day War against Israel, which cost it the Golan Heights and exposed the young regime's military weakness.",
